MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root-caused the 'no tracking, no km' report:
- The driver's active-rental application had its car_id dropped again by
  the Marketplace website's owner unmatch/rematch flow (same class of bug
  as before) — useActiveRental never resolved, so the background location
  task never even registered. Fixed the data directly so testing can
  continue; this needs a fix on the Marketplace side to stop recurring.
- driver_live_status hadn't updated in 4 days even during a window where
  the car_id *was* valid, pointing to Android (Samsung especially)
  killing the background location foreground service to save battery —
  a well-known limitation with no error surfaced anywhere in the app, so
  it looks identical to 'tracking is broken' from the outside. Added a
  one-tap 'Fix Battery Settings' prompt (expo-intent-launcher +
  expo-application) that requests exemption from battery optimization,
  shown once per install after permission is otherwise granted. This is
  the practical mitigation available without a full native rewrite — it
  can't force the OS to comply, but it's the standard fix for this class
  of Android background-service killing.
- The map only ever renders driver_live_status as-is; its 'inaccurate'
  position was this same stale-data symptom, not a separate map bug.

Also moved DrivingSafetyCard from the Activity tab to the Rental tab per
request (own tab or part of Rental) — avoids duplicating it in two
places.
